{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Premise VALIDATED against current main, and sharper than filed.\n\nBaseline, this worktree (macOS 15, pandoc 3.6.1 via pypandoc-binary==1.15), module in isolation:\n\n| run | wall | CPU (user+sys) | fills |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| serial (`-p no:randomly`) | 135.09s | 86.79s | ONE 47.92s fill |\n| `-n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300` | 92.03s | 143.46s | THREE fills: 44.49s / 43.38s / 42.82s |\n\nSo yes: three per-worker cache fills under xdist where serial pays one, +56.7s of CPU re-deriving an identical artifact. Aggregate per-test time under the CI command was 211.45s.\n\nA second duplication the ticket did not name: the three `passes_two_to_five` tests each recomputed `render_markdown_to_wiki(body)` for pass 1 — bit-for-bit the value `_rendered()` already held.\n\nAFTER (same commands, same machine):\n\n| run | wall | CPU (user+sys) | largest fill |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| serial | 70.00s (-48%) | 51.23s (-41%) | 37.50s |\n| `-n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300` | 62.80s (-32%) | 74.58s (-48%) | 17.24s (-61%) |\n\nAggregate per-test time under the CI command: 211.45s -> 82.73s, **-61%**. Largest single test 44.49s -> 17.24s, far under the 300s hang guard and under the 120s AC bar. 11 passed in both runs; no test skipped or deleted; all 178 bodies still rendered by real pandoc.\n\nImplementation note / plan divergence: a single whole-corpus artifact was tried first and REGRESSED wall clock (92.03s -> 115.06s) because two workers idled ~42s waiting on the winner, even though CPU fell to 93.07s. Sharding the artifact per stratum with a `PYTEST_XDIST_WORKER`-rotated probe order fixed that: workers fill different shards concurrently, so the cold-session cost is one stratum (~17s) rather than the whole corpus. The description was updated to match before this comment."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786603480309849001,"uuid":"640e2610-772d-4b17-80b3-7509041d0026"}